// A top-level block in script mode is a statement: it runs in the
// synthesized main, in order with the statements around it. It used to be
// dropped without a word (the first println printed 1). Oracle: the same
// statements inside `int main()`, compiled by gcc and clang, print "3" and
// then "in block 30".
int g = 1;
{ int t = 2; g = g + t; }
println("{}", g);
{
	g = g * 10;
	println("in block {}", g);
}
